  "result": "Perfect! All 224 tests pass, including 23 new credit notes tests. Here's what I added:\n\n**`src/credits.js`** (new file)\n- `createCreditNote(invoice, { amount, reason, date }, existingNumbers)` function that:\n  - Validates invoice status is `'issued'`, `'partially_paid'`, or `'paid'` (returns `NOT_ISSUED` error for draft)\n  - Validates amount is a positive integer (returns `AMOUNT_INVALID` error)\n  - Validates amount doesn't exceed invoice total (returns `CREDIT_TOO_HIGH` error)\n  - Generates credit note number with format `CN-YYYY-NNNN` with independent counter\n  - Returns `ok(creditNote)` with: `{ number, invoiceNumber, customerId, amount, reason, date }`\n\n**`src/errors.js`** (updated)\n- Added `CREDIT_TOO_HIGH` error code\n- Updated `NOT_ISSUED` error message to cover credit notes\n\n**`test/credits.test.js`** (new file)\n- 23 comprehensive tests covering:\n  - Basic credit note creation for all valid statuses (issued, partially_paid, paid)\n  - Error validation (draft invoices, invalid amounts, exceeding total)\n  - Credit note numbering (separate counter from invoices, year-based)\n  - Handling mixed invoice and credit note numbers\n  - Multiple credit notes per invoice\n  - Year boundaries and counter resets\n  - Integration with invoices that have discounts\n\nCredit notes are properly numbered independently from invoices, allowing both `INV-2026-0001` and `CN-2026-0001` to coexist.",
